# suse64 — SuSE Linux 6.4 i386 (2000-03). Reset = loadvm golden on disk.qcow2, the
# only block device (rule 6: golden + /opt/qemu-beos binary + device set are one).
# Checkpoint (2026-09-03 08:58 box time, KVM, /opt/qemu-beos): savevm golden VM_SIZE 84.1 MiB,
# VM_CLOCK 0:16:02.407; staged from /data/gallery-guests/SUSE64/suse64-rn.qcow2 (892 MiB on disk).
# The scene is the RETRONET one: GtkICQ 0.60 signed in as UIN 18000 with HiveBot online in
# its contact list, the kpanel along the bottom, the konsole beside it, and Netscape 4.72 in the taskbar having
# already rendered http://search.retronet/. Device set is TWO ne2k_pci NICs (slirp eth0 with
# restrict=on, tap suse64rn0 eth1 = 10.99.0.37) — docs/lab/retronet/STATION-suse64.md.
# Guest: UP kernel 2.2.14 (k_deflt) + hdparm -d1 (DMA on, 58.7 MB/s), XFree86 3.3.6 SVGA
# clgd5446 no_bitblt 1024x768x16, tty1 autologin -> startx -> startkde, one konsole.
SH_RESET_MODE=loadvm
SH_GOLDEN_SNAPSHOT=golden
SH_GOLDEN_STATE_DISK=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/suse64/disk.qcow2
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=SuSE Linux 6.4 KDE 1.1.2 desktop (XFree86 3.3.6 SVGA on Cirrus, 1024x768x16): console autologin into startx, a konsole and GtkICQ signed in to the retronet with HiveBot online, Netscape Communicator 4.72 one click away in the taskbar. Pointer motion absolute through the guest X server (x11warp), buttons + keys over PS/2.
# Fleet floor for QEMU keyboard stations; measure only if characters drop.
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=40
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=40
SUSE64_QEMU=/opt/qemu-beos/bin/qemu-system-x86_64
# Pointer: motion via XWarpPointer + XQueryPointer readback on the guest's X
# server, reached through the launcher's loopback SLIRP forward (6080 -> 6000).
# The golden carries `xhost +10.0.2.2`. Buttons/keys: D-Bus PS/2 (default path).
SH_INPUT_BACKEND=x11warp
SH_X11WARP_DISPLAY=127.0.0.1:80
SH_X11WARP_TRACE=off
SH_CURSOR_SCALE=1.0
